\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Principal hourly result. (A) On 521,424 common exact-date cells with a shared 423-date factor, generative methods sharply reduce sparse-cell RMSE relative to direct and bootstrap expansion; station-cluster uncertainty is shown for the contrastive-versus-direct effect. (B) Pooling dates removes that advantage in absolute volume. (C) Contrastive training improves normalized hourly shape relative to its ablation, while the Bayesian network is best.}}{12}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hourly}{{5}{12}{Principal hourly result. (A) On 521,424 common exact-date cells with a shared 423-date factor, generative methods sharply reduce sparse-cell RMSE relative to direct and bootstrap expansion; station-cluster uncertainty is shown for the contrastive-versus-direct effect. (B) Pooling dates removes that advantage in absolute volume. (C) Contrastive training improves normalized hourly shape relative to its ablation, while the Bayesian network is best}{figure.5}{}}
